      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-07T17:01:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They come originally from the H1 chip spec. However, the current version of the spec has suggested values based on a 26 MHz bus clock and H1 is at 24 MHz. In addition, for 100 and 400 kHz, I have made phase0 longer because the external pullups are too weak. I have an ask of gchips to get me updated suggested values for 24 MHz.\n\nI have tested at 100 and 400 kHz. I can\u0027t test 1000 at this time because the rise time on both Reef and Gru is too slow (\u003e iuSec) to run at that speed. I have highlighted the issue to HW team. Since Reef only has 4 INAs, if I get stronger pullups then I may be able to test 1000 kHz.\n\nAdded a TODO comment to document the current state.",
      "parentUuid": "1fd62c37_562094b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 3
      },
